WEBVTT

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:44.030
Stand by Good afternoon.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:49.020
This Meeting of the Huntsville City Council will come to order.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:54.120
I am President Pro Tem Bill Kling, and with me are council members David

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.630
Little and Michelle Watkins.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:57.950
Excuse me.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:02.520
The purpose of this special session is for the purpose of canvassing the

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.600
returns of the municipal runoff election that was held on September 22nd.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:13.940
I am now going to turn the program meeting rather over to the city clerk

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.170
for the county of provisional ballots.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.200
Good afternoon, counsel and to all joining online and in the council chambers.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.010
Today we will be counting the provisional ballots that require further review

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.560
by the board of registrars.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.650
Council, there were 7 provisional ballots,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:38.600
and of those 75 have been accepted to be counted towards our official results

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.170
of the September 22nd runoff election.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.320
And at this time, we will begin counting those ballots,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.460
and I will announce each candidate.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:54.140
You can explain how Counsel, I will pass the ballot down to you.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.280
For our first ballot, Jenny Robinson.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.110
For a 2nd ballot, Jenny Robinson.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.010
For our 3rd ballot, Jenny Robinson.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:24.280
For our 4th ballot, Liliana Pender and counsel,

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.880
for your records, this ballot has been torn and we will have to manually

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.720
load the results.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.200
It will not feed in the DS 200 machine.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.950
It will when we update the official numbers that you see on the screen.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.180
IT is here present and he will update manually before I read the final results.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:05:01.260
And for our 5th and final ballot, which this ballot council is also torn,

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.380
we will load the results manually, and it is Liliana Pender.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.240
And that will conclude the reading of all of our provisional ballots.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:18.450
And at this time, we will allow our IT team to update the official election

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:23.370
night reporting system, and then I will read the final numbers into the

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:23.750
record.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:52.190
Counsel, while we wait on the election night reporting system to update,

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.760
Councilman Klean asked me to explain this process,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:06:00.030
and I think it's important to understand provisional ballots.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:04.480
If they are accepted, it means that they voted in the precinct and it needed

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.710
further review by the board of registrars.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:12.970
Oftentimes, someone may be at the wrong precinct and those are rejected.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.850
You must be in your correct precinct in order for your ballot to be cast.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:23.240
And also, you could be missing an ID and you have an opportunity at a later

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.530
date to present that to the board of registrars.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.790
Also, if you vote absentee in my office, but Because of mail or for whatever

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.190
reason, your absentee ballot did not make it back in time,

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:40.500
you still have an opportunity for your ballot to be cast by voting provisional

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.520
in the precinct.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:45.800
And so we take time to work with the board of registrars to ensure that

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.620
every vote counts and there's a thorough review,

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.930
uh, before today's canvassing.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.630
Councilor McLean, is there anything else you wanted me to explain?

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.140
OK.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.880
Any other questions from the council members?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.320
OK.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.570
We will wait on the system to update as we close the polls.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:46.800
For those who might have turned into Tuned into this broadcast that we are

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:51.990
having, we are in the process of counting the provisional ballots that were

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:55.120
not counted as part of the.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:01.690
District 3 runoff election that was held and we're getting the official

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:06.270
numbers and the final tally will be totaled up shortly.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:13:48.400
Hm Thank you, Tom.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:56.370
Before we get started, I do want to say to the Madison County staff,

00:13:56.460 --> 00:14:01.660
thank you to the board of registrars, IT probate Judge Frank Barger and

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:08.950
his staff, ESNS, and our circuit clerk for their support during this 2026

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.890
municipal election cycle.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:14.650
Um, it would not be possible without the collaboration,

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.170
and I just want to on the record thank them.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:22.020
And thank my entire team that's in here today and those that are absent

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.450
and on a well-deserved vacation.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:28.960
Uh, thank you and to the council for being here today as we wrap up.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:33.380
Our results are ready and at this time, council,

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:43.550
for the record, Liliana Pender received 47.64% with 3,436 votes.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:53.240
Jenny Robinson, 52.36% with a total of 3,776 votes.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:58.270
And at this time, council, I will officially turn it over to you for new

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:00.470
business items for consideration.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:01.100
Thank you.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:01.670
Thank you.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.350
I might add for those who are in the council chambers,

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:10.460
the individual box totals are a point on the billboard over there for your

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:11.270
inspection.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:22.860
Uh, council members, uh, is there a motion concerning OK.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:26.840
Is there a motion concerning declaring Jenny Robinson,

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.130
District 3 City council, City of Huntsville,

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.610
elected to her position for a term beginning November 2,

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:35.860
2026?

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:36.880
Move to approve.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:41.010
Second motion has been made and properly seconded.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:41.900
Discussion.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.330
All those in favor signify by saying aye,

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:51.800
aye, and the chair votes aye, uh, hereby declare Jenny Robinson is the winner

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:56.880
of the District 3 city council race of the city of Huntsville,

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:57.720
Alabama.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.810
If there's no other business, we're adjourned.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:02.640
Thank you.
